The '''2026 {{Lang|es|La Vuelta Femenina|italic=no}}''' (officially '''{{Lang|es|La Vuelta Femenina|italic=no}} by Carrefour.es''') was the fourth edition of {{Lang|es|[[La Vuelta Femenina]]|italic=no}}, a cycling [[stage race]] that took place in [[Spain]]. The race ran from 3 to 9 May, and was the 16th event in the [[2026 UCI Women's World Tour]]. From 2026, more ranking points will be awarded at the [[Giro d'Italia Women]], [[Tour de France Femmes]] and the Vuelta Femenina – elevating these races in status compared to other races in the UCI Women's World Tour.<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 June 2025 |title=Part II Road Races - Amendments to Regulations as from 20.10.2025 |url=https://assets.ctfassets.net/761l7gh5x5an/NAeT9EN3grfH1b8uTXoYv/8b18929d380cb33fbb62d3efd3a71f27/2-ROA-20251020-E-amendments_on_20.10.25.pdf |access-date=20 June 2025 |website=[[Union Cycliste Internationale]] |page=15 |quote=2.10.017 Points scale Women Elite}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Price |first=Matilda |date=2025-06-20 |title=UCI points update brings Women's WorldTour system in line with men's, designating women's Monuments and boosting Tour de France Femmes |url=https://www.cyclingnews.com/news/uci-points-update-brings-womens-worldtour-system-in-line-with-mens-designating-womens-monuments-and-boosting-tour-de-france-femmes/ |access-date=2025-06-20 |website=Cyclingnews |language=en}}</ref>

The race was won by Spanish rider [[Paula Blasi]] of {{UCI team code|UAD women|2026a}}, taking the overall victory and the mountains classification after an attack on the final stage of the race to [[Alto de l'Angliru|l'Angliru]]. Second overall was Dutch rider [[Anna van der Breggen]] of {{UCI team code|SDW|2026}}, who had taken the leaders jersey after a win on stage 6. Third overall was French rider [[Marion Bunel]] of {{UCI team code|TVL women|2026}}, with Bunel also winning the youth classification as the best placed rider under the age of 23. The points classification was won by Belgian rider [[Lotte Kopecky]] of {{UCI team code|SDW|2026|nolink=y}}, with {{UCI team code|SDW|2026|nolink=y}} also taking the teams classification.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ostanek |first=Dani |last2=Frattini |first2=Kirsten |date=2026-05-03 |title=La Vuelta Femenina final GC standings – A new face in the red jersey on the final day as the Angliru decides overall victory |url=https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/womens-cycling/la-vuelta-femenina-gc-standings-2026/ |access-date=2026-05-18 |website=Cyclingnews |language=en}}</ref>

